UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — Her Senate bio and available issue statements show only generic deregulation/pro-Trump-agenda/tax-cut rhetoric, with no documented action or statement on whether government should offer, limit, or refuse business-attraction incentives. Direction (pro-business, low-tax) does not establish a position on this incentive-offering axis, so no chair fits. Left blank: no chair on this incentive axis fits the documented record.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://moody.senate.gov/about$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='f6c97c43-41e3-45ae-bdaa-c339f2e6ed4d' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- Ashley Moody
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — Chisholm's sponsored bills (repealing utility surcharges, 'Freedom From Monopolies Act,' co-sponsoring a broad-based corporate tax rate cut) reflect a deregulatory, market-competition philosophy opposed to government-directed programs generally, but none of them is evidence of a stance on whether government should offer incentive packages to attract employers, or fund small-business programs instead. A deregulator who opposes subsidies on free-market grounds does not fit chair 1 (progressive public-investment) or chair 5 (actively offering the largest unconditional incentives) -- these describe opposite motivations. No chair fits. Left blank: no chair on this incentive axis fits the documented record.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Members/Details/chisholm01$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='cfc704da-dd6c-40b0-97fa-0c5ece8d3976' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- Brian Chisholm
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — The only documented quote is her defense of a federally (BLM-grant) funded parks/pickleball project against calls to redirect it to housing -- a dispute about how to spend an existing federal land-sale grant, not about whether the city should offer tax breaks, subsidies, or incentive packages to attract businesses. No source found addresses the business-incentive axis at all. Left blank: no chair on this incentive axis fits the documented record.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://news3lv.com/news/local/las-vegas-pickleball-project-sparks-debate-over-federal-spending$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='91544dd2-07c7-4885-943f-f431836ddecf' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- Francis Allen-Palenske
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — His sponsored/co-sponsored bills (Office of Regulatory Management regulatory-reduction bill; HB0690 Economic Competitiveness Act, a broad-based corporate income tax RATE cut applying to all businesses) show a deregulation and broad tax-rate-cut posture, not a documented position on offering (or refusing) targeted incentive packages to attract specific employers. Broad-based tax cuts are off the incentive-conditionality axis the v2 scale measures, so no chair fits. Left blank: no chair on this incentive axis fits the documented record.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Legislation/Details/hb0690?ys=2026RS$u$,$u$https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Members/Details/stonko01$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='656a8bc9-348e-4ffc-819c-2f4611b3ddc8' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- Joshua J. Stonko
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — His record (Freedom From Monopolies Act deregulating retail energy supply; bills exempting tips, overtime pay, and precious-metal sales from tax; a co-sponsored data-center moratorium) is about deregulation and broad tax exemptions, not about offering, conditioning, or refusing targeted business-attraction incentives. No evidence places him on the v2 incentive-conditionality spine, so he does not fit any chair. Left blank: no chair on this incentive axis fits the documented record.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Legislation/Details/hb0974?ys=2026RS$u$,$u$https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Members/Details/fisher?tab=2026RS-legislation$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='71542618-59c8-4b06-a765-e3df60cca763' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- Mark N. Fisher
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — His sponsored bills are local Anne Arundel County matters (a rural-legacy property tax credit, a residential property tax deferral, a barbershop/salon alcohol license bill, and school/fire-company bond bills) plus a broad sales-tax exemption for precious metals — none document a position on offering or opposing incentive packages to attract employers. The prior 'championed deregulation and tax cuts as core Republican platform' reasoning was a party-line inference rather than incentive-specific evidence, so this topic is left blank.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Members/Details/kipke?tab=2026RS-legislation$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='0e0bdc53-b5a2-4292-aeb7-341a4c5bed08' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- Nicholaus R. Kipke
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — His signature bill, the Property Rights Protection Act (HB1550), repeals eminent domain/condemnation authority — a property-rights position, not a stance on whether government should offer tax breaks or subsidies to attract employers. His other bills (a broad corporate tax rate cut, a precious-metals sales-tax exemption, unemployment-fraud enforcement) are likewise off the incentive-conditionality axis, so no chair is supported by the evidence. Left blank: no chair on this incentive axis fits the documented record.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Legislation/Details/hb1550?ys=2026RS$u$,$u$https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Legislation/Details/hb0690?ys=2026RS$u$,$u$https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Members/Details/grammer01$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='0608cc7a-72ed-4d24-b966-3eee82075bf1' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- Robin L. Grammer, Jr.
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — His Senate issues page explicitly frames growth as coming from low taxes, minimal regulation, and right-to-work laws 'without the federal government getting in the way,' and his flagship Main Street Certainty Act is a broad-based, economy-wide small-business tax deduction, not a targeted incentive package for specific employers. This is the free-market-deregulator pattern the v2 scale explicitly excludes: he neither documents redirecting money to public investment (chair 1) nor documents offering (even unconditionally) the largest incentives to attract a specific large employer (chair 5), so no chair fits and the topic is left blank pending evidence of an actual incentive-package position.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://tuberville.senate.gov/issues/economy-fiscal-responsibility/$u$,$u$https://www.ontheissues.org/Tommy_Tuberville.htm$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='7affca4e-db2b-4f7e-b009-9acc6b493139' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- Tommy Tuberville
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — Only available record is a vague campaign statement about wanting to 'grow the tax base and partner with the private sector' -- this names no specific incentive action, subsidy, or business-attraction program and cannot be placed on the incentive-conditionality axis. No chair fits without guessing. Left blank: no chair on this incentive axis fits the documented record.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='f51c85d1-88b2-4a44-8c68-0cd0e72bd2bd' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- Bill Smitz
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — Brammer's record consists of broad-based state income and gas tax cuts, which are off-axis general tax policy rather than a targeted incentive/subsidy package aimed at attracting a major employer. His own framing -- crediting growth to 'cutting taxes' and favoring market-driven development over government incentive programs -- points away from, not toward, actively offering large incentives, so chair 4 is unsupported and no other chair is evidenced either. Left blank: no chair on this incentive axis fits the documented record.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://utahnewsdispatch.com/2024/02/29/utah-legislature-income-tax-cut/$u$,$u$https://atr.org/utah-enacts-6th-income-tax-cut-in-6-years-and-shaves-6-cents-off-gas-tax/$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='070c1c1c-ac9d-42e0-bff2-3f4467504cba' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- Brady Brammer
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — West's sponsored bills (corporate law modernization, digital asset regulation, online gambling enforcement) are regulatory/legal matters off the incentive axis, and his co-sponsored Rural Readiness Program/Capacity Building Fund provides community-level planning capacity to rural areas rather than a subsidy or tax break aimed at a specific large employer. No named incentive-package action exists to support chair 4 or any other chair. Left blank: no chair on this incentive axis fits the documented record.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Members/Details/west02$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='fc06c2bb-db76-43fa-8e2e-91a4c34e57ae' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- Chris West
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — Adams co-sponsored the Rural Readiness Program/Capacity Building Fund, which builds rural communities' planning capacity rather than subsidizing a specific large employer, plus a broad corporate tax-rate cut and a noncompete/employer-relocation labor bill (withdrawn) -- none of which is a named large-incentive package to attract major employers. Evidence does not establish chair 4 or any other chair on this axis. Left blank: no chair on this incentive axis fits the documented record.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Members/Details/adams01$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='1eada938-f28c-46b9-bd21-df241656cd2b' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- Christopher T. Adams
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — Maack's stated priority is fiscal restraint -- line-by-line spending control to lessen the tax burden -- pursued explicitly 'without new resources,' which is a general tax/spending posture rather than a position on offering or withholding subsidies and incentives to attract employers. This does not map onto the new incentive-focused scale, so no chair fits the available evidence. Left blank: no chair on this incentive axis fits the documented record.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://racinecountyeye.com/2024/02/08/david-maack-racine-alder-candidate/$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='359c3243-f328-4cfd-b13a-0c319acf1b6d' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- David L. Maack
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — Cefalu-Paulick's platform is limited to general deregulation language -- 'supporting small businesses and reducing unnecessary burdens' -- with no mention of any tax-break, subsidy, or incentive program in either direction. Pure regulatory-burden rhetoric without a named incentive stance does not place her on this incentive-focused scale, so no chair fits. Left blank: no chair on this incentive axis fits the documented record.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://www.wisconsinrightnow.com/gina-paulick/$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='1d3dabab-3ecf-46e0-8a5e-34be8a7d27b9' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- Gina Cefalu-Paulick
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — Sosa's comments focus entirely on permitting and bureaucratic reform -- 'unnecessary level of bureaucracy and red tape' and departments needing to 're-invent the way they process applications' -- with no reference to tax breaks, subsidies, or incentive packages of any kind. This is deregulation, not an incentive-spending stance, so it is off-axis for the new scale and no chair fits. Left blank: no chair on this incentive axis fits the documented record.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://downeylatinonews.com/en/2022/10/ask-the-candidates-hector-sosa$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='92d68971-8cc2-480b-8e29-9938f7a280f1' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- Hector Sosa
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — Gallion's one clearly documented economic-development sponsorship, a Rural Readiness Program/Rural Maryland Capacity Building Fund bill, could not be verified in full text and its mechanism (infrastructure/capacity building vs. direct company subsidy) is unclear from available sources. The evidence does not clearly establish where he falls on the incentives-to-attract-employers axis, so no chair confidently fits. Left blank: no chair on this incentive axis fits the documented record.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Members/Details/gallion01$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='e2ca1bfd-255d-417b-a9d7-424e6c10749d' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- Jason C. Gallion
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — No documented evidence of Obernolte offering, sponsoring, or championing a specific tax-abatement/subsidy package to attract a major employer. His record here is a general free-market, anti-stimulus, anti-mandate posture (opposing the PRO Act and the American Rescue Plan, campaigning on low taxes/limited government), which is off-axis for a scale measuring how far government goes to hand companies incentives — a broad deregulation philosophy does not equal actively offering (or refusing) incentive packages, so no chair is supported by the evidence. Left blank: no chair on this incentive axis fits the documented record.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://www.ontheissues.org/CA/Jay_Obernolte_Jobs.htm$u$,$u$https://www.ontheissues.org/CA/Jay_Obernolte_Budget_+_Economy.htm$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='18db5d61-6bce-4f55-ad45-bed01f329548' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- Jay Obernolte
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — Boozman's record on business subsidies is general fiscal conservatism (limiting federal spending growth, an earmark moratorium, opposing debt-limit increases) rather than a named incentive package used to recruit a major employer to Arkansas; his one documented subsidy-related vote (opposing removal of existing oil & gas exploration subsidies) protects an existing tax provision rather than actively offering a new incentive to attract an employer. Without a specific abatement, TIF, or recruitment deal on record, his general deregulatory/anti-spending posture does not place him on this incentive-to-attract-employers axis, so no chair is supported. Left blank: no chair on this incentive axis fits the documented record.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://www.ontheissues.org/Senate/John_Boozman.htm$u$,$u$https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Boozman$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='3621bbef-a821-45fe-991c-e1744ad05203' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- John Boozman
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — Mautz's economic record is deregulation and protection of existing Eastern Shore industries against mandates and taxes (opposing the $15 minimum wage as too aggressive for local business owners, opposing the statewide paid-family-leave mandate, requiring referendum approval for county income-tax authority, and seeking tariff protection for the Chesapeake seafood industry), with no named tax-abatement or subsidy package used to attract a major outside employer. This anti-mandate/protectionist posture does not correspond to any rung on an axis measuring how far government goes to hand companies incentives to attract them, so no chair is supported. Left blank: no chair on this incentive axis fits the documented record.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johnny_Mautz$u$,$u$https://mgaleg.maryland.gov/mgawebsite/Members/Details/mautz01$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
 WHERE politician_id='34c94aa4-11b7-4594-9c3e-c506f10309f6' AND topic_id='eb3d1247-0de1-4b7f-baec-7259861efd53'; -- Johnny Mautz
UPDATE inform.politician_context SET reasoning=$ctx$Researched 2026-09-01 — Husted's documented record is deregulation and cost-cutting (reduced Ohio business startup costs 21% as Secretary of State; used AI to strip 5 million words from the regulatory code as Lt. Governor) rather than any named tax-abatement, subsidy, or incentive package offered to attract a specific large employer. Under the v2 scale this is off-axis -- a free-market deregulator without a documented incentive deal does not fit chair 4, so this is left blank rather than guessed.$ctx$, sources=ARRAY[$u$https://husted.senate.gov/about/$u$,$u$https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jon_Husted$u$]::text[], editor_id='854fbc06-40fc-458d-b523-20ef8e5ad1b2', updated_at=now()
